# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Template for obsidian.env — created by scripts/setup.sh, which fills the hostname and
# generates the GUI credentials. Copy by the script rather than by hand; the two secret
# values are the ones a fresh stack cannot reuse.

# ─── The public name ───
# The hostname Caddy answers and takes a certificate for. Written down once, here.
WIKI_HOSTNAME=wiki.example.org

# ─── The publisher's boundary ───
# These are Anthers' publish decision, stated in the environment so the server needs no
# build-time knowledge of them. Another operator publishing their own vault states their own.
# Defaults live in src/server/services/boundary.ts and match these exactly; setting them here
# makes the running stack's boundary readable without opening the code.
PUBLISH_EXCLUDE=Internal Wiki,90-99 Agents,00-09 Metafiles
PUBLISH_INCLUDE=00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks
PUBLISH_BASE_FILES=Anthers Tasks.base

# ─── The vault Sync pulls (obsidian-headless) ───
# The sync engine joins your Obsidian Sync account as one more device and keeps the vault
# copy current; the server reads that copy. The mode is the publisher's posture —
# mirror-remote downloads only and reverts any local change, so this machine can never
# become a vault editor even by accident.
VAULT_NAME=Anthers-Wiki
DEVICE_NAME=anthers-wiki
SYNC_MODE=mirror-remote
# Config syncing off — this machine never receives .obsidian/ material; it isn't the app's.
SYNC_CONFIGS=
# 🚨 **This list is the sync-layer half of the publish boundary — belt to the server's
# boundary suspender, and both wear it.** The server refuses to serve anything outside its
# publish boundary even if this list were empty; this list is what keeps the internal
# material from ever *arriving* on a machine whose only job is to be public. Keep it in
# step with PUBLISH_EXCLUDE below: the boundary decides what the server will serve, this
# decides what the folder will hold — and if you widen one without the other, the wider
# one is your true boundary. Write that down rather than discovering it in a log.
EXCLUDED_FOLDERS=Internal Wiki,90-99 Agents,00-09 Metafiles/00 Attachments,.obsidian,.trash,.stfolder,.stversions,.agents

# The two credentials arrive as files, not values — a value here would appear in
# `docker inspect`, a mode-0600 file on the 0700 secrets directory does not.
# Both are your own acts, in your own terminal:
#   printf %s '<token>'    > ${OBSIDIAN_DIR}/secrets/obsidian_token   # (from `make sync-token`)
#   printf %s '<password>' > ${OBSIDIAN_DIR}/secrets/vault_password   # (the vault's E2E password)
# If you would rather pass a credential directly, name it here as the plain value
# (OBSIDIAN_AUTH_TOKEN, VAULT_PASSWORD) and leave the _FILE line for it empty — but the
# files are the better shape. Setting both a plain value and its _FILE is an error the
# sync engine reports at start.
OBSIDIAN_AUTH_TOKEN_FILE=/secrets/obsidian_token
VAULT_PASSWORD_FILE=/secrets/vault_password

# ─── Where the stack's state lives on the host ───
# setup.sh creates it. Everything the stack keeps — the vault copy, the sync engine's
# identity and index — is under this one directory, so backing it up is one cp.
OBSIDIAN_DIR=/srv/anthers-obsidian